module BackwardPipeOperatorRowComment exposing (..)

-- A `{- -}` written in front of a `<|` rides the operator's row (rule C3). When
-- the previous body ends in a `--`, that operator drops to a row of its own --
-- and the comment must come with it, still IN FRONT of it. Gluing it onto the
-- end of the line the operator sits on put it on the far side (`<| {- c -}`),
-- which the reparse reads as leading the OPERAND and moves again.


midChainBlockComment =
    alpha <|
        beta -- trails the second body
        {- rides the operator -} <|
            gamma


-- The comment-free twin: the `<|` drops for the `--` alone, so the comment
-- changes nothing but its own presence on that row (rule C4).


midChainNoComment =
    alpha <|
        beta -- trails the second body
        <|
            gamma


-- A run of them, and a chain long enough that the step below still nests one
-- tab stop deeper than the one above it.


midChainCommentRun =
    alpha <|
        beta -- trails the second body
        {- one -} {- two -} <|
            gamma <|
                delta


-- One the author wrote AFTER the operator leads the operand instead, and so
-- travels down to the operand's row. The two sides of the gap are the one thing
-- about a comment here that is NOT interchangeable, and erasing the difference
-- is what made the shape above oscillate.


afterTheOperator =
    alpha <|
        beta -- trails the second body
        <|
            {- follows the operator -} gamma
